Dynamical systems interpretation
For a trajectory or collective system, the point cloud itself is already a representation. Euclidean distance may ignore temporal order, periodic coordinates, anisotropic units or dynamically meaningful similarity. A defensible analysis therefore states:

the observed scientific object and how the points were constructed;
the metric or dissimilarity;
the complex and scale convention;
whether clique filling represents a plausible higher-order relation; and
what simpler geometric or graph baseline the topological result must beat.

