TipWhat to retain before returning



A vector space has a stated field of scalars. A basis gives coordinate columns but is not the same thing as the underlying vectors. A matrix represents a linear map relative to chosen bases. Kernels record erased input directions; images record attainable outputs; rank and nullity count their independent directions. A quotient declares a specified difference irrelevant.


